<title>POLAND: Dahl buys 49 pct of Polish trader-paper.</title>
<headline>Dahl buys 49 pct of Polish trader-paper.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish wholesaler Dahl, Scandanavia's largest wholesaler in the heating industry, bought a 49-percent stake in Polish trader Tadmar SA, the financial daily Nowa Europa reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Tadmar President Marek Bykowski told the paper that his firm, based in Poznan, western Poland, owns four large wholesale outlets in northern and western Poland and plans to use Dahl investment to set up outlets throughout the country.</p>
<p>He said largely Polish goods would be sold there.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
